# MCO Wizard - Visual SNLP Generator
# Core configuration for orchestrating Cascade to build the MCO Wizard

@workflow "Creating a Visual 'MCO workflow' creation tool"
> This workflow orchestrates the creation of the MCO Wizard, a visual tool for building and managing MCO SNLP files.

@description
> A visual SNLP generator that allows users to create, customize, and validate MCO workflows through an intuitive, modern interface.
> The tool supports pre-built templates, community workflows, and building from scratch with real-time validation.

@version "0.0.1"

# Data Section - Core data structures and initial state
@data:
  project_description: "A visual SNLP generator that allows users to create, customize, and validate MCO workflows through an intuitive, modern interface. The tool supports pre-built templates, community workflows, and building from scratch with real-time validation. The MCO Wizard tool should be developed with the intention of being able to easily add pre-built and community built workflows, whether by a github integration or other. Whichever the method, a developer guide, and user guide alike should be included, the user-guide as an element that is able to be toggled into view via the UI in the frontend, and the developer guide being a .md file in the projects backend/source codebase."
  core_functionality: "1. Browse and select from pre-built and community workflows 2. Customize existing workflows by editing values and NLP sections 3. Create new workflows from scratch with guided structure 4. Real-time validation of SNLP syntax and structure 5. Download validated SNLP files individually or as a package 6. Preview how progressive revelation will work in the final workflow"
  technical_requirements: "1. Frontend: Modern web framework (React/Vue) with responsive design 2. Backend: Real validation using the same logic as the MCO CLI validation tool 3. File handling: Generate and download valid SNLP files 4. Storage: Local storage for user workflows and preferences 5. Integration: API endpoints for future community workflow repository"
  development_approach: "Build the application incrementally, focusing first on the core SNLP editing experience, then adding workflow management features, and finally implementing the validation and community features. Use component-based architecture for maintainability and extensibility."
> This data block provides the core context, requirements, and definitions needed for the agent to build the MCO Wizard application.

# Agents Section - Define the agents involved in the workflow
@agents:
  Cascade:
    model: "N/A - Windsurf IDE"
    description:
    > You are Cascade, the Windsurf IDE integrated coding agent. You're tasked with creating "MCO Wizard" - a visual SNLP generator that makes creating MCO workflows intuitive and accessible.
    > You excel at creating clean, modern web interfaces with excellent UX/UI.
    > You understand the MCO protocol deeply and can implement its validation rules accurately.
    tools: []

# Workflow Steps Section - The sequence of actions for the workflow
@workflow_steps:
  setup_frontend_project:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Set up a new React project using Create React App. Install necessary dependencies like styled-components for styling and an icon library."
    output: "frontend_project_structure"

  design_core_ui_components:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Design and implement the core UI components: a file navigator sidebar, a main content editor view, and a validation status bar. Use modern, clean design principles."
    input: "{frontend_project_structure}"
    output: "ui_components"

  implement_file_loading:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Implement the logic to read the SNLP files from the backend and display their content in the editor view when a file is selected in the navigator."
    input: "{ui_components}"
    output: "file_display_logic"

  enable_realtime_editing:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Connect the editor view to the application state so that user modifications are tracked in real-time."
    input: "{file_display_logic}"
    output: "editing_state_management"

  integrate_validation_engine:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Integrate the SNLP validation logic from the backend. As the user types, send the content to the validation engine and display any errors or warnings in the validation status bar."
    input: "{editing_state_management}"
    output: "live_validation_feature"

  implement_file_download:
    agent: "Cascade"
    task: "Create a feature to allow users to download the currently edited SNLP files, either individually or as a complete package."
    input: "{live_validation_feature}"
    output: "download_functionality"

# Error Handling Section - How to manage failures
@error_handling:
  syntax_validation_error:
    condition: "Validation engine returns an error"
    action: "Display the specific error message and line number to the user in the UI, highlighting the problematic line in the editor."

  file_not_found:
    condition: "A required SNLP file (mco.core, mco.sc) cannot be loaded from the backend"
    action: "Display a critical error modal in the UI, preventing further action until the files are available."

